"""Jobs for the reading-room exploration, ROUND TWO: eight concepts where reading a pod is research at the Station (the instrument and the act of reading
as an experiment), each with its matching incubators as the same family of instrument (several units on one bench, with room for more).
usage: python3 -I tools/readroomexplore2jobs.py   -> writes source/work/concepts-readroom-explore-2/jobs-<id>.json, one job each, 1K, 16:9, one try.
Run each with: python3 -I tools/gen.py source/work/concepts-readroom-explore-2/jobs-<id>.json (the Pacific-day total checked before each)."""
import json, os
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); ROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)
WORK = os.path.join(ROOT, "source/work/concepts-readroom-explore-2"); os.makedirs(WORK, exist_ok=True)
MODEL = "gemini-3-pro-image"
REFS = [
    [os.path.join(ROOT, "source/work/concepts-readroom/ref-pod-loika.png"),
     "THE POD (project-owned game art): a wild seed pod, slate-blue with a round coral cap, pale vertical ribs and coral dots. Keep its design exactly wherever a pod appears; never make it a jar, a vase, a lantern or an egg of another design."],
    [os.path.join(ROOT, "source/work/concepts-readroom/ref-loika.png"),
     "THE CREATURE (project-owned game art): the Loika the pod will become: a small round charcoal creature with a cream belly and muzzle, amber eyes, four stubby legs with pale toes and three green leaves on its head. Keep its design exactly; never invent another creature."],
    [os.path.join(WORK, "ref-station-finish.png"),
     "THE STATION'S FINISH (one of our own screens, project-owned): its incubator, a matte dark slate capsule with a glass dome, a warm lamp inside and a moss nest, standing on a quiet sage wall with soft painted light. Take the rendering: matte, soft, warm, painted, real depth, a handled instrument. Today's incubator is this capsule; the new one in the picture may be of the same family but of the concept's own form."],
    [os.path.join(WORK, "ref-station-frame.png"),
     "THE STATION'S HOUSING (one of our own screens, project-owned): the sage powder-coated housing with recessed screws, a braided black hose with brass fittings, and the dark soft tray inside where the pod stands. This is the material language of every instrument in the picture: sage and sand housing, dark rubber, screws, braided hose, dark matte slate displays. Take the materials, not the layout."],
]
HEAD = ("Paint the WHOLE screen of a creature-keeping game played on a handheld home research station, 16:9, a mood-and-layout thumbnail for a concept: the READING ROOM, "
        "where the player reads a wild pod (a seed pod with a creature's genome sleeping inside) one chapter at a time, as an EXPERIMENT on a research bench. "
        "The feeling: a pod is RICH IN SURPRISES, there is more inside than can be seen, and each read brings one out into the light. The place is a LAB THAT IS A HOME: "
        "a naturalist's field kit on a warm evening, cosy because it is handled and loved, never a cold laboratory, never a cottage. "
        "ALSO IN THE PICTURE, smaller, the station's INCUBATORS as the same family of instrument as the reading instrument (same housing, same materials, same maker), "
        "two or three units on the same bench and a free mount or bay where another unit could be added: one incubator holds a glowing bud growing in warm light, one is empty and dark, the free mount has only its hose fitting. ")
TAIL = ("\nLIGHT AND FINISH: one warm key light from the top left, soft cast shadows, soft contact shadows, a few small lit marks on the instruments that mean something (a lamp on a working unit, nothing lit for show). "
        "Matte, painted, miniature finish like the reference screens; the instruments are quiet matte sage, sand, dark rubber and dark slate; the colour lives in the pod's inner light, the surprises and the life. "
        "No gloss, no chrome, no neon, no holograms, no glowing outlines, no sci-fi interface, nothing childish, no wooden furniture, no books, no candles, no cottage.\n"
        "NO text, letters, digits, numbers, logos, buttons, panels or icons anywhere (the game types its words later). No frame, no border, no vignette; the picture fills the canvas edge to edge.")
CONCEPTS = {
 "strand": "CONCEPT: THE STRAND (a sequencer). The pod is seated in a cradle on the left of a long bench, and a soft glowing STRAND is drawn out of it along a shallow channel that runs right across the middle of the screen, like tape through a reader. The strand is two threads twisted gently round each other, and along it sit many small frosted BEADS, each glowing faintly its own colour (russet, amber, cream, ash, green): the unread chapters, plenty of them, the strand long and full. A small sage read-head with a dark rubber hood sits over one bead, and under the head that bead is clear and bright and shows a tiny picture: a lock of russet fur. Where the strand ends at the right it runs into the small Loika standing on a dark pad, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog, the fur part just coloured. Behind the bench, low and small, the family's incubators: two cylindrical sage units with glass fronts on the same rail as the reader, one lit warm with a bud inside, one dark, and a third bare mount with a braided hose fitting.",
 "spectrum": "CONCEPT: THE SPECTRUM (a spectrometer). The pod stands on a dark cradle at the lower left, lit from inside, and its glow passes through a small matte-sage slit housing and a glass prism, and opens out to the right as a wide FAN OF SOFT COLOURED BANDS across a large dark matte slate screen that fills the right two thirds of the picture. There are many bands, each a different soft colour (russet, amber, cream, ash, green, slate): the unread chapters, a full spectrum. The bands are soft and blurred except ONE, where a thin sage needle on a rail stands: that band is sharp and holds a picture, a lock of russet fur, and under it a thinner fainter twin band is just coming clear. Below the screen, on the bench, the small Loika sits looking up at the fan of light, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog. Along the bottom edge of the bench, small, the family's incubators: squat sage boxes with a glass lid and a slit lamp of their own, one lit warm with a bud, one dark, and a bare mount beside them.",
 "sweep": "CONCEPT: THE SWEEP (a scanner). The pod lies on its side in a shallow sage scanner bay at the left third of the screen, under a clear hood, and a thin bar of warm light is passing slowly over it, lighting a stripe of the shell. On a large dark matte slate screen filling the right two thirds, the pod's cross-section is drawn as if by the sweep, stripe by stripe: the outer shell as a soft outline and INSIDE it, nested at different depths, many soft coloured shapes still blurred and grainy like an unfinished scan (a tuft of fur, a round eye, a paw, a leaf, a curl of tail), with ONE shape, the fur, drawn clear and bright where the sweep has passed, and a fainter ghost of it just beneath. The screen's lower corner shows the small Loika, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog. Below the scanner bay, stacked, the family's incubators: two more bays of the same sage housing with clear hoods, one lit warm with a bud lying inside, one empty and dark, and a bare slot with a braided hose fitting.",
 "column": "CONCEPT: THE COLUMN (a separation column). A tall glass column in a sage frame stands in the centre of the screen, nearly its full height, lit warm from behind so it glows. The pod stands at the top in a cradle, and from its foot a drop of its glow falls into the column; in the column the light SEPARATES as it sinks into many soft stacked BANDS of colour, each settling at its own height (russet, amber, cream, ash, green, slate), the upper bands still cloudy and moving, the lower ones settled: the unread chapters, a column full of them. A sage collector ring on a rail round the column sits at one band, and that band is sharp and holds a picture, a lock of russet fur, with a thin brighter line just under it. At the column's foot, on a dark pad, the small Loika sits, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog, with a trickle of warm light reaching it. To the right, smaller, the family's incubators: two glass tubes in the same sage frames, one lit warm with a bud held inside, one dark, and a bare frame with a braided hose fitting.",
 "candle": "CONCEPT: THE CANDLE (candling). The pod is held in a dark rubber cradle at the centre of the screen, huge, and a strong warm lamp behind it shines THROUGH the shell so the pod is translucent like a candled egg: the slate-blue shell becomes deep amber glass and inside it, seen as soft silhouettes in the glow, many curled sleeping SHAPES are visible (a tuft of fur, a round eye, a paw with toes, a leaf, a curl of tail, a pair of ears), nested, overlapping, plenty of them, each with a faint hint of its colour. ONE shape, the fur, turned to the front, is lit sharp and shows its true russet colour through the shell. The cradle sits in a sage housing with recessed screws and a braided hose, and the lamp's hood is matte sage. At the lower right, small, the Loika sits on a dark pad looking at the pod, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog. At the lower left, smaller, the family's incubators: two cradles of the same housing each with its own lamp behind, one holding a translucent bud glowing warm, one dark and empty, and a bare third cradle.",
 "tank": "CONCEPT: THE TANK (a specimen tank with sensors). A round glass tank in a sage frame fills the centre of the screen, filled with clear warm water that glows softly, and the pod rests in the middle of it on a dark pad, lit from within. Around the pod, clipped to the tank's rim in a ring, several small sage sensor probes with dark rubber grips lean in, each with a tiny lamp, and from one probe a soft ripple spreads through the water and where the ripple passes a soft picture forms in the water, a lock of russet fur, with a fainter second ring behind it. The water is full of many tiny drifting lit motes in different soft colours (russet, amber, cream, ash, green), like plankton: the unread chapters, a tank rich with them. The small Loika sits on the bench at the lower right pressing its nose to the glass, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog. To the left, smaller, the family's incubators: two smaller round tanks in the same frames, one lit warm with a bud floating inside, one dark and drained, and a bare ring mount with a braided hose fitting.",
 "plates": "CONCEPT: THE PLATES (a light table). A wide light table in a sage frame fills the picture: its surface a large pale matte glass lit warm from beneath, and clipped on it with dark rubber clips a loose group of translucent PLATES, each a shadowgram of the pod. The pod itself stands at the lower left on a dark cradle at the table's edge, lit from inside. Most plates are DARK and undeveloped, with only a soft coloured blur of what they hold (russet, amber, cream, ash, green): the unread chapters, many plates. ONE plate has developed: it shows the pod as a soft silhouette with a lock of russet fur lit clear inside it, and a fainter second image of the fur ghosting just beside. At the lower right, small, the Loika sits on the table's edge, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog. Along the table's back edge, smaller, the family's incubators: two low sage drawers with glass tops lit from beneath like the table, one lit warm with a bud inside, one dark, and a bare empty slot with a braided hose fitting.",
 "field": "CONCEPT: THE FIELD (a microscope). A bench microscope in sage housing with dark rubber knobs stands at the left, its lens over the pod, which sits on the stage lit from below. The right two thirds of the screen is the microscope's FIELD: a huge round view on a dark matte slate screen, showing the pod's shell surface at great magnification: a soft pattern of overlapping scales and cells in slate-blue and coral, and set into the pattern many small bright SEEDS, each a different soft colour (russet, amber, cream, ash, green), each with a tiny shape sleeping in it: the unread chapters, a field full of them. The field is soft and slightly out of focus except at its centre, where one seed is sharp and open and shows a lock of russet fur, with a second smaller seed just beside it coming clear. At the lower right, small, the Loika sits on the bench under the screen, half painted in colour and half soft grey fog. Along the bench at the lower left, smaller, the family's incubators: two small sage domes with stages of their own lit from beneath, one lit warm with a bud, one dark, and a bare stage with a braided hose fitting.",
}
for cid, text in CONCEPTS.items():
    job = {"name": f"concepts-readroom-explore-2/{cid}", "model": MODEL, "aspect": "16:9", "size": "1K", "tries": 1, "refs": REFS, "prompt": HEAD + text + TAIL}
    json.dump([job], open(os.path.join(WORK, f"jobs-{cid}.json"), "w"), indent=1)
    print("wrote", f"jobs-{cid}.json")
